<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $268.7 mln March 25.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $268.7 mln March 25.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $268.7 million deficit on March 25 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 25</p>
<p>Exports: $278.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $329.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $157.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $375 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $268.7 million</p>
<p>MARCH DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.525 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.598 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.855 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.716 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $66 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
</text>
